{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Kronecker","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose_pos","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L129-L138","doc":"**Positivity is preserved by juxtaposition** (over a linearly ordered ring): if both component\namplitudes are positive so is the composite. Together with `markovTrace_juxtapose` this supplies BOTH\nhypotheses of `QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge.freeEnergy_connectedSum` — multiplicativity and\npositivity — from the juxtaposition structure alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L119-L127","doc":"**Non-vanishing is preserved by juxtaposition** — the composite amplitude of two non-vanishing\ncomponents is non-vanishing (needed for the archimedean `log`, where the amplitude must be nonzero\nbefore the free energy is defined). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.trace_kron_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.trace_kron_self","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L113-L117","doc":"**A self-juxtaposed block squares its trace.** Two-fold only; for `A` components see\n`QOU.Mass.ClosureNormalisationDefect.closureNorm_assemble`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose_one","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L90-L103","doc":"**A `1×1` identity block is the unit of the Kronecker product at the trace level.** Its trace is\n`1` because `Fintype.card Unit = 1`.\n\n🛑 This is a statement about the INDEX TYPE, not about strands (bean `qou-bsfg`). Adding an unlinked\ncomponent to a braid closure multiplies the amplitude by the **loop value** `δ = [2]_q`, not by `1`:\nat `q₀` that is `δ = 2.01089686671`, i.e. `log δ = 0.6985808249` of free energy per component. See\n`QOU.Mass.ClosureNormalisationDefect.freeEnergy_closureNorm_juxtapose`. The lemma below is true and\nuseful for matrices; do not read it as \"a trivial component is free\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.markovTrace_juxtapose","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L81-L88","doc":"**Markov-trace multiplicativity under juxtaposition.** If the composite evaluation is the\njuxtaposition of two blocks, its trace factorises as the product of the block traces. This is the\nalgebraic form of `J(K₁ # K₂) = J(K₁) · J(K₂)` (Jones 1987) — and it is the hypothesis that\n`QOU.Mass.ArchimedeanTraceBridge` carries, here discharged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.IsJuxtaposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.IsJuxtaposition","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L75-L79","doc":"A **juxtaposition** (disjoint-strand product) of two block evaluations: the composite matrix `C`\nis the Kronecker product of the blocks. This is the algebraic content of \"the two sub-braids share no\nstrand\", i.e. of the connected sum / distant union in the Hecke tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.trace_kron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceMultiplicative.trace_kron","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTraceMultiplicative.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**The trace is multiplicative under the Kronecker product.** Restatement of\n`Matrix.trace_kronecker` in the form the Markov-trace application uses: the amplitude of a\ndisjoint (non-interacting) union is the product of the amplitudes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}